IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 (Cth), Chapter 4A (vaping goods) -- what counts as vaping goods (s 41P); importing (s 41Q),
-- making (s 41QA) and supplying (s 41QB) them; possessing at least a commercial quantity (s 41QC); possessing less than a
-- commercial quantity at retail premises (s 41QD); and the retail-pharmacy route by which vaping goods may lawfully be
-- supplied to a person (s 41QB(9)-(12)).
--
-- SEAT: the minor found with a vape (Jake, at 16). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Are these vaping
-- goods?", "Is my possession an offence?", "Was the shop's sale to me an offence?", "May a pharmacist lawfully supply me?",
-- "Would bringing one in from overseas, or making my own liquid, be an offence?". Where the Act hands a matter to the
-- Minister (s 41R determinations, s 41RA indications), the Secretary (s 41RC consents) or a State law (Schedule 3 authority,
-- the supplier's State authority under s 41QB(11)(c)(ii)), the answer is conditional on that matter, asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3(1) ("supply", "pharmacist", "medical practitioner", "nurse practitioner", "commercial quantity",
-- "manufacture"), s 41N (as a comment), s 41P(1), (3), s 41Q(1)-(3), (5), s 41QA(1)-(3), (5), s 41QB(1)-(3), (5)-(12),
-- s 41QC(1)-(14), s 41QD(1)-(10), s 41QE (as a comment), s 41R, s 41RA.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 89 (register id C2025C00525), compilation date 5 September 2025, includes amendments up to Act
-- No. 38, 2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03952.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026). Chapter 4A was
-- added by the Therapeutic Goods and Other Legislation Amendment (Vaping Reforms) Act 2024 (No. 50, 2024), Schedule 1 in
-- force 1 July 2024 (endnotes). No regulations are deposited: the "commercial quantity" (s 3(1)) and the "permitted
-- quantity" (s 41QD(10)) of a kind of vaping goods are prescribed by the Therapeutic Goods Regulations 1990 and are INPUTS
-- here. Penalties are stated in penalty units; the value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA and is not
-- used.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Chapter 4A's advertising rules (Part 5-1A); breach of a consent condition (s 41RD); the consent procedure
-- (ss 41RB, 41RC) beyond whether a consent is held; executive officer liability (ss 54B, 54BA); the State law that governs
-- a pharmacist's or doctor's authority to supply (the Poisons Standard schedules and the WA medicines law are not read);
-- the Customs Act 1901 prohibition that s 41Q(5) borrows; the supply route through a carer (s 41QB(11)(a)(ii)); and every
-- other Chapter of the Act. Whether the sale to a person under 18 offends the Tobacco and Other Products Control Act 2006
-- (WA) is that Act's question; its text is not deposited.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 (Cth), Chapter 4A`

§§ `numbers and helpers`

-- Endnotes: No. 50, 2024, "sch 1: 1 July 2024". Chapter 4A (ss 41N-41RD) is "ad No 50, 2024".
`the day Chapter 4A began` MEANS Date 1 7 2024

GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chapter 4A was in force on` MEANS Day `d` AT LEAST Day `the day Chapter 4A began`

§§ `41P -- are these vaping goods`

-- s 41P(1): "vaping goods means any of the following goods: (a) a vaping substance; (b) a vaping accessory; (c) a vaping
-- device; (d) goods the presentation of which includes an express or implied representation that the goods are of a kind
-- referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c); (e) goods that are ... determined to be vaping goods under subsection (3)."
-- "vaping substance" (a)(i) "nicotine in solution in any concentration" or (ii) "any liquid or other substance for use in,
-- or with, a vaping device" -- so a nicotine-free liquid for a vape is a vaping substance.
-- "vaping accessory means a cartridge, capsule, pod or other vessel ... for use in, or with, a vaping device".
-- "vaping device" generates "using a heating element and by electronic means, an aerosol, vapour or mist for direct
-- inhalation"; the Note gives humidifiers, diffusers, nebulisers and inhalers as devices that are not.
-- s 41P(3): the Minister may determine that specified goods "are or are not vaping goods".
DECLARE `Kind of goods` IS ONE OF
    `a vaping substance (nicotine in solution, or any liquid for a vaping device)`
    `a vaping accessory (a cartridge, capsule, pod or other vessel for a vaping device)`
    `a vaping device (an electronic heated aerosol device for inhalation)`
    `goods presented as a vaping substance, accessory or device`
    `goods the Minister has determined are vaping goods`
    `goods the Minister has determined are not vaping goods`
    `a humidifier, diffuser, nebuliser or inhaler`
    `something else`

@export Are these vaping goods under the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 s 41P?
GIVEN `what they are` IS A `Kind of goods` @desc What the goods are
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are these vaping goods` IF
    CONSIDER `what they are`
    WHEN `goods the Minister has determined are not vaping goods` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a humidifier, diffuser, nebuliser or inhaler` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `the standing of the goods and of the person`

-- ss 41QB(6), (9), 41QC(13), 41QD(7), in the same words: "(a) the vaping goods are therapeutic goods that are entered on the
-- Register; or (b) ... exempt goods ... and the sponsor has given the Secretary a notice in compliance with the exemption;
-- [and] the vaping goods are not the subject of a determination by the Secretary ... that the supply of the goods be stopped
-- ...; or (c) the vaping goods are covered by a determination made by the Minister under section 41R."
DECLARE `Standing of the goods` IS ONE OF
    `entered on the Register`
    `exempt, with the sponsor's notice given, and not stopped by the Secretary`
    `covered by a Minister's s 41R determination`
    `none of those`

GIVEN `s` IS A `Standing of the goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the goods have standing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `none of those` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 41QC(14) lists who may hold vaping goods: (a) an importer under a Customs Act s 50 licence and permission or approval;
-- (b) a Part 3-3 manufacturing licence holder; (c) a conformity assessment document holder; (d) "a wholesaler, pharmacist,
-- medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who is the holder of a licence, or is otherwise authorised, to supply one or
-- more substances included in Schedule 3 to the current Poisons Standard", possessing "in accordance with the licence or
-- authority"; (e) a Secretary's consent under s 41RC(1), possessing in accordance with it; (f) a person specified in a
-- s 41R determination, possessing in accordance with it. s 41QD(8) keeps only the pharmacist/doctor/nurse practitioner limb
-- of (d), the consent and the determination.
DECLARE `My authority` IS ONE OF
    `no authority`
    `an import licence and permission, or approval, under the Customs Act s 50 regulations`
    `a Part 3-3 manufacturing licence for a step in making them`
    `a conformity assessment document for them`
    `a wholesaler's State Schedule 3 authority, acting within it`
    `a pharmacist's, doctor's or nurse practitioner's State Schedule 3 authority, acting within it`
    `the Secretary's consent under s 41RC, acting within it`
    `a s 41R determination naming me, acting within it`

GIVEN `a` IS A `My authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is an authority s 41QC(14) recognises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a`
    WHEN `no authority` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `a` IS A `My authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is an authority s 41QD(8) recognises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a`
    WHEN `a pharmacist's, doctor's or nurse practitioner's State Schedule 3 authority, acting within it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Secretary's consent under s 41RC, acting within it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a s 41R determination naming me, acting within it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `41QC, 41QD -- my possession`

-- One holding of one kind of vaping goods, as the person could describe it. The commercial quantity and the permitted
-- quantity are prescribed by regulations that are not deposited; they are inputs, in the same unit as the quantity held.
-- s 41QE: "the person bears an evidential burden" for any exception; here every exception fact is simply asked.
DECLARE `My vaping goods` HAS
    `what they are`                                     IS A `Kind of goods`
    `the date I held them`                              IS A DATE
    `how much I hold`                                   IS A NUMBER    -- of one kind, in the regulations' unit
    `the commercial quantity for that kind`             IS A NUMBER    -- s 3(1): prescribed by the regulations
    `the permitted quantity for that kind`              IS A NUMBER    -- s 41QD(10): prescribed by the regulations
    `their standing`                                    IS A `Standing of the goods`
    `my authority`                                      IS A `My authority`
    `I am a retailer holding them at the retail premises` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 41QD(1)(a), (b), (10)
    `they are for my own personal use`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 41QC(11A)(b), s 41QD(9)(a)
    `they were lawfully supplied to me`                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 41QC(11A)(a)
    `my age in years`                                   IS A NUMBER    -- read by nothing: the Act names no age

-- ss 41QC(1), (4), (7), 41QD(1): the bands are fixed by multiples of the commercial quantity.
DECLARE `Quantity band` IS ONE OF
    `less than the commercial quantity`
    `at least the commercial quantity but less than 100 times it`
    `at least 100 times but less than 1,000 times the commercial quantity`
    `1,000 times the commercial quantity or more`

GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods`
GIVETH A `Quantity band`
`Which quantity band am I in` MEANS
    IF `g`'s `how much I hold` LESS THAN `c`
    THEN `less than the commercial quantity`
    ELSE IF `g`'s `how much I hold` LESS THAN 100 TIMES `c`
         THEN `at least the commercial quantity but less than 100 times it`
         ELSE IF `g`'s `how much I hold` LESS THAN 1000 TIMES `c`
              THEN `at least 100 times but less than 1,000 times the commercial quantity`
              ELSE `1,000 times the commercial quantity or more`
    WHERE `c` MEANS `g`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`

-- s 41QC(11A): "Subsections (1) to (3) and (10) and (11) do not apply ... if: (a) the vaping goods have been lawfully
-- supplied to the person; and (b) the vaping goods are for use by the person personally; and (c) the quantity is less than
-- 5 times the commercial quantity". It does not reach the 100-times and 1,000-times offences (subsections (4)-(9)).
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 41QC personal-use exception applies` MEANS
        `g`'s `they were lawfully supplied to me`
    AND `g`'s `they are for my own personal use`
    AND `g`'s `how much I hold` LESS THAN 5 TIMES `g`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`

-- s 41QC(12): "Subsections (1) to (11) do not apply if subsections (13) and (14) apply".
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the s 41QC general exception applies` MEANS
        `the goods have standing` (`g`'s `their standing`)
    AND `it is an authority s 41QC(14) recognises` (`g`'s `my authority`)

@export Is my possession of vaping goods an offence under s 41QC (at least a commercial quantity)?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my possession a commercial-quantity offence` IF
        `Chapter 4A was in force on` (`g`'s `the date I held them`)
    AND `Are these vaping goods` (`g`'s `what they are`)
    AND `g`'s `how much I hold` AT LEAST `g`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`
    AND (NOT `the s 41QC general exception applies` `g`)
    AND (NOT (    `Which quantity band am I in` `g` EQUALS `at least the commercial quantity but less than 100 times it`
              AND `the s 41QC personal-use exception applies` `g`))

-- s 41QD(1): "the person is a retailer in relation to retail premises in Australia; and ... possesses a quantity of a kind
-- of vaping goods at the retail premises; and ... the quantity is less than the commercial quantity".
-- s 41QD(10): "retailer" is an owner, lessee or occupier of retail premises, a person conducting a business there, their
-- director, officer or agent, or "a person performing work in any capacity (including ... an employee or a contractor)"
-- for them there. A customer who is none of these is not a retailer.
-- s 41QD(6)-(8): no offence if the goods have standing and the person holds a recognised authority.
-- s 41QD(9): no offence if "the vaping goods are for use by the person personally" and "the quantity is not more than the
-- permitted quantity".
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an s 41QD exception applies` MEANS
        (    `the goods have standing` (`g`'s `their standing`)
         AND `it is an authority s 41QD(8) recognises` (`g`'s `my authority`))
    OR  (    `g`'s `they are for my own personal use`
         AND `g`'s `how much I hold` AT MOST `g`'s `the permitted quantity for that kind`)

@export Is my possession of vaping goods an offence under s 41QD (less than a commercial quantity, at retail premises)?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my possession a retail-premises offence` IF
        `Chapter 4A was in force on` (`g`'s `the date I held them`)
    AND `Are these vaping goods` (`g`'s `what they are`)
    AND `g`'s `I am a retailer holding them at the retail premises`
    AND `g`'s `how much I hold` LESS THAN `g`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`
    AND (NOT `an s 41QD exception applies` `g`)

DECLARE `What my possession is` IS ONE OF
    `outside Chapter 4A: these are not vaping goods`
    `outside Chapter 4A: it was not yet in force (it began on 1 July 2024)`
    `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity`
    `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises`
    `no offence: an exception applies`
    `no offence: less than the commercial quantity and I am not a retailer at retail premises`

-- The seat's question. s 41N: "the manufacture, supply or possession of vaping goods in Australia, is prohibited, subject to
-- some exceptions" -- but the possession offences reach only a commercial quantity (s 41QC) or a retailer at retail
-- premises (s 41QD). Below the commercial quantity, a person who is not a retailer commits no possession offence under this
-- Act, whatever their age.
@export Is my possession of vaping goods an offence under the Therapeutic Goods Act 1989?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A `What my possession is`
DECIDE `Is my possession of vaping goods an offence` IS
    IF NOT `Chapter 4A was in force on` (`g`'s `the date I held them`)
    THEN `outside Chapter 4A: it was not yet in force (it began on 1 July 2024)`
    ELSE IF NOT `Are these vaping goods` (`g`'s `what they are`)
         THEN `outside Chapter 4A: these are not vaping goods`
         ELSE IF `Is my possession a commercial-quantity offence` `g`
              THEN `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity`
              ELSE IF `Is my possession a retail-premises offence` `g`
                   THEN `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises`
                   ELSE IF     `g`'s `how much I hold` AT LEAST `g`'s `the commercial quantity for that kind`
                            OR `g`'s `I am a retailer holding them at the retail premises`
                        THEN `no offence: an exception applies`
                        ELSE `no offence: less than the commercial quantity and I am not a retailer at retail premises`

-- Penalties for the possession offences, individual. s 41QD(1): "Imprisonment for 12 months or 500 penalty units";
-- (3) strict liability "60 penalty units"; (4) civil "for an individual -- 1,000 penalty units", per unit held (s 41QD(5)).
-- s 41QC(1): "Imprisonment for 2 years or 1,000 penalty units"; (3) "120 penalty units"; (4): "4 years or 3,000";
-- (6) "240"; (7): "7 years or 5,000"; (9) "420"; (10) civil "for an individual -- 7,000 penalty units", per unit (s 41QC(11)).
@export What is the longest prison term, in months, for my possession of vaping goods?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest prison term in months for my possession` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my possession of vaping goods an offence` `g`
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises` THEN 12
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity` THEN
        CONSIDER `Which quantity band am I in` `g`
        WHEN `at least 100 times but less than 1,000 times the commercial quantity` THEN 48
        WHEN `1,000 times the commercial quantity or more` THEN 84
        OTHERWISE 24
    OTHERWISE 0

@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, for the fault-based offence for my possession of vaping goods?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine in penalty units for my possession` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my possession of vaping goods an offence` `g`
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises` THEN 500
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity` THEN
        CONSIDER `Which quantity band am I in` `g`
        WHEN `at least 100 times but less than 1,000 times the commercial quantity` THEN 3000
        WHEN `1,000 times the commercial quantity or more` THEN 5000
        OTHERWISE 1000
    OTHERWISE 0

@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, for the strict liability offence for my possession of vaping goods?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest strict liability fine in penalty units for my possession` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my possession of vaping goods an offence` `g`
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises` THEN 60
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity` THEN
        CONSIDER `Which quantity band am I in` `g`
        WHEN `at least 100 times but less than 1,000 times the commercial quantity` THEN 240
        WHEN `1,000 times the commercial quantity or more` THEN 420
        OTHERWISE 120
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The civil penalty provisions share the offences' exceptions: s 41QC(11A) reaches (10) and (11), s 41QC(12) reaches
-- (1)-(11), and s 41QD(6) and (9) reach (1)-(5). The personal-use exception's ceiling (under 5 times the commercial
-- quantity) means it can never reach a holding of 100 times or more, so the civil exposure follows the offence.
@export What is the most civil penalty, in penalty units per unit of vaping goods, I can be ordered to pay for my possession?
GIVEN `g` IS A `My vaping goods` @desc The vaping goods you hold and the facts about them
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most civil penalty per unit for my possession` IS
    CONSIDER `Is my possession of vaping goods an offence` `g`
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QD: a retailer, less than the commercial quantity, at retail premises` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an offence under s 41QC: at least the commercial quantity` THEN 7000
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `41QB -- the supply to me`

-- s 3(1): "supply includes ... supply by way of sale, exchange, gift, lease, loan, hire or hire-purchase" and supply "free
-- of charge ... by way of sample".
-- s 41QB(10): "(a) the person is a pharmacist; or (b) the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who is the
-- holder of a licence, or is otherwise authorised, to supply one or more substances included in Schedule 3 to the current
-- Poisons Standard under a law of the State or Territory in which the supply occurs."
DECLARE `Supplier` IS ONE OF
    `a pharmacist`
    `a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner with State Schedule 3 authority`
    `a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner without it`
    `a shop or anyone else`

-- s 41QB(11)(a)(i): "for use by that person for smoking cessation, management of nicotine dependence or another indication
-- determined by the Minister under section 41RA".
DECLARE `Purpose of the supply` IS ONE OF
    `smoking cessation`
    `managing nicotine dependence`
    `an indication the Minister has determined under s 41RA`
    `any other use`

DECLARE `The supply to me` HAS
    `what was supplied`                                       IS A `Kind of goods`
    `the date of the supply`                                  IS A DATE
    `it was supplied in Australia`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `its standing`                                            IS A `Standing of the goods`
    `who supplied it`                                         IS A `Supplier`
    `the supplier holds an authority s 41QB(7) recognises`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- importer, manufacturer, wholesaler, consent, determination
    `I hold an authority s 41QB(8) recognises`                IS A BOOLEAN  -- recipient licence, Schedule 3 authority, consent, determination
    `what it was supplied for`                                IS A `Purpose of the supply`
    `it is or contains a vaping substance`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the substance is in final dosage form`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 41QB(12)
    `the supply complies with the rest of the Act and the supplier's State authority` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 41QB(11)(c)

-- s 41QB(5)(a), (6)-(8): the wholesale supply chain. The recipient must be a licensed manufacturer, a wholesaler,
-- pharmacist, doctor or nurse practitioner with State Schedule 3 authority, hold a Secretary's consent to supply, or be
-- named in a s 41R determination.
GIVEN `s` IS A `The supply to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the wholesale-chain exception covers it` MEANS
        `the goods have standing` (`s`'s `its standing`)
    AND `s`'s `the supplier holds an authority s 41QB(7) recognises`
    AND `s`'s `I hold an authority s 41QB(8) recognises`

GIVEN `p` IS A `Purpose of the supply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a purpose s 41QB(11) allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `p`
    WHEN `any other use` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `w` IS A `Supplier`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a retail supplier s 41QB(10) allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `w`
    WHEN `a pharmacist` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner with State Schedule 3 authority` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 41QB(5)(b), (9)-(12): the retail supply chain. (11)(b): "if the vaping goods are, or contain, a vaping substance -- the
-- vaping substance is in final dosage form"; (12): "a form that can be administered to a person without any change or
-- modification (other than vaporisation)". (11)(c): "(i) in accordance with this Act (apart from this section); and (ii)
-- consistent with the person's authority to supply the vaping goods under a law of the State or Territory".
@export Did the supply of vaping goods to me fall within the retail (pharmacy) exception of s 41QB(9)-(11)?
GIVEN `s` IS A `The supply to me` @desc Who supplied you, what, and for what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the supply to me within the retail exception` IF
        `the goods have standing` (`s`'s `its standing`)
    AND `it is a retail supplier s 41QB(10) allows` (`s`'s `who supplied it`)
    AND `it is a purpose s 41QB(11) allows` (`s`'s `what it was supplied for`)
    AND (    (NOT `s`'s `it is or contains a vaping substance`)
          OR `s`'s `the substance is in final dosage form`)
    AND `s`'s `the supply complies with the rest of the Act and the supplier's State authority`

-- s 41QB(1): "A person commits an offence if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia." (5): subsections (1)-(4) do not
-- apply if (6), (7) and (8), or (9), (10) and (11), apply.
@export Was the supply of vaping goods to me an offence by the supplier under s 41QB?
GIVEN `s` IS A `The supply to me` @desc Who supplied you, what, and for what
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the supply to me an offence` IF
        `Chapter 4A was in force on` (`s`'s `the date of the supply`)
    AND `Are these vaping goods` (`s`'s `what was supplied`)
    AND `s`'s `it was supplied in Australia`
    AND (NOT `the wholesale-chain exception covers it` `s`)
    AND (NOT `Was the supply to me within the retail exception` `s`)

-- What may lawfully be supplied to me, as far as the Act says: a pharmacist (or an authorised doctor or nurse practitioner)
-- may supply goods with standing, for one of the three purposes, in final dosage form, consistently with the State law.
-- The Act sets no age limit; whether the State law allows supply to a person under 18 is asked as a fact.
@export May a pharmacist lawfully supply me vaping goods under s 41QB?
GIVEN `the goods' standing` IS A `Standing of the goods` @desc Whether the goods are on the Register, notified exempt goods, or covered by a Minister's determination
      `what I want them for` IS A `Purpose of the supply` @desc What the goods would be supplied to you for
      `they are in final dosage form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any vaping substance can be used without change other than vaporisation
      `the State law lets the pharmacist supply me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supply is consistent with the pharmacist's authority under State law (including any age or prescription rule)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a pharmacist lawfully supply me vaping goods` IF
        `the goods have standing` `the goods' standing`
    AND `it is a purpose s 41QB(11) allows` `what I want them for`
    AND `they are in final dosage form`
    AND `the State law lets the pharmacist supply me`

-- s 41QB(1): "Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both"; (2) strict liability "200 penalty units";
-- (3) civil "for an individual -- 7,000 penalty units; and ... for a body corporate -- 70,000 penalty units", and (4) a
-- separate contravention "in respect of each unit of vaping goods supplied".
-- The 5,000 penalty units are the Act's figure for the offence; any multiplier for a body corporate comes from the
-- Crimes Act 1914, which is not read.
@export What is the largest fine, in penalty units, the seller faces for the s 41QB supply offence?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine in penalty units for the seller` IS 5000

@export What is the longest prison term, in years, the seller faces for the s 41QB supply offence?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest prison term in years for the seller` IS 7

@export What is the most civil penalty, in penalty units per unit supplied, the seller can be ordered to pay under s 41QB(3)?
GIVEN `the seller is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller is a company rather than an individual
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most civil penalty per unit for the seller` IS
    IF `the seller is a body corporate` THEN 70000 ELSE 7000

§§ `41Q, 41QA -- bringing them in, or making them, myself`

-- s 41Q(1): "A person commits an offence if the person imports vaping goods into Australia." (5): "Subsections (1) to (4)
-- do not apply if the importation of the vaping goods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901." That Act is not read;
-- whether it prohibits the importation is asked.
@export Would importing vaping goods into Australia myself be an offence under s 41Q?
GIVEN `what they are` IS A `Kind of goods` @desc What the goods are
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the importation
      `the Customs Act 1901 prohibits the importation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the importation is prohibited under the Customs Act 1901 (for example, without a licence and permission)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would importing vaping goods myself be an offence` IF
        `Chapter 4A was in force on` `the date`
    AND `Are these vaping goods` `what they are`
    AND `the Customs Act 1901 prohibits the importation`

-- s 41QA(1): "manufactures, or carries out a step in the manufacture of, vaping goods". s 3(1) "manufacture" includes "to
-- produce the goods" or engage in any part of the process, "including ... processing, assembling, packaging, labelling".
-- (5): no offence if "the vaping goods are therapeutic goods" and the person holds a Part 3-3 licence for the site, a
-- conformity assessment document, or a Secretary's consent and acts within it.
@export Would making vaping goods (for example, mixing my own liquid) be an offence under s 41QA?
GIVEN `what they are` IS A `Kind of goods` @desc What the goods are
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the manufacture
      `they are therapeutic goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods are therapeutic goods
      `I hold a licence, conformity document or consent for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Part 3-3 licence for the site, a conformity assessment document, or a Secretary's consent and act within it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would making vaping goods myself be an offence` IF
        `Chapter 4A was in force on` `the date`
    AND `Are these vaping goods` `what they are`
    AND (NOT (`they are therapeutic goods` AND `I hold a licence, conformity document or consent for it`))
